<title>HUNGARY: Hungary stat. office releases March CPI breakdown.</title>
<headline>Hungary stat. office releases March CPI breakdown.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-04-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hungary's Central Statistical Office (KSH) released detailed March consumer price index (CPI) figures on Friday.</p>
<p>HUNGARY'S CONSUMER PRICE INDEX (CPI) -- PCT CHANGE</p>
<p>			 March '97     Feb '96	March '96</p>
<p> Month-on-month     +1.9	   +2.2	    +1.9</p>
<p> Year-on-year	+18.8	   +18.8	   +25.6</p>
<p>CPI PCT CHANGE IN MAIN PRODUCT GROUPS</p>
<p>				March 1997		Weight in</p>
<p>			    mth/mth   yr/yr	   index (pct)</p>
<p> Food products	    0.9     14.5		28.6</p>
<p>Alcoholic</p>
<p>beverages/</p>
<p>  tobacco products	0.6     19.8		 9.0</p>
<p> Clothing		   1.7     20.7		 6.3</p>
<p>Durable consumer</p>
<p>  goods		     0.5	8.9		 6.2</p>
<p> Household energy	 8.1     37.8		 8.0</p>
<p> Other goods, fuels     0.6     19.0		17.0</p>
<p> Services		   2.8     19.4		24.9</p>
<p> Total			1.9     18.8	     100.0</p>
<p>NOTE - The CPI was boosted by government measures by 1.1 percent within the total 1.9 percent monthy-on-month rise in March, the KSH said.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom (36 1) 327 4040</p>
</text>
